"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"ST014\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that an AP must be a member or participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency and have a written agreement with the ETF or one of its service providers to place creation and redemption orders.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Names the AP and distributor as common counterparties. It omits the transfer agent's countersignature and the trust's status as third-party beneficiary, and says it cannot identify the reviewed forms' parties.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Says only that forms 'may impose more specific NSCC/DTC eligibility.' It does not describe NSCC netting membership for the clearing process versus DTC participation outside it, and does not say eligibility differs from market-maker status.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Required coverage is 2.0 of 3, which meets the half threshold. There is no central error: 'the trust/fund may also be a party' is a generic, hedged statement and does not claim the trust is the main signatory in the reviewed forms. Points 2 and 3 are substantively incomplete, so the grade is partial.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":3886,"type":"result","duration_ms":6988,"uuid":"62cd00cf-62ed-4d81-bdfd-041d3b909d39","ttft_stream_ms":1597,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1598,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
